# Pin line endings to LF for every text file.
#
# Two things in this repository depend on it:
#
#   1. Pinned evidence logs. `examples/kitchen-sink/spikeB-proxy/proxy-log.jsonl`
#      is committed evidence whose line count (730) is asserted by the Spike F
#      re-verification checklist, and the replay harness splits it on '\n'.
#      A CRLF checkout would produce false failures against real evidence.
#
#   2. The canonical serializer golden. PRD §14.3 fixes a trailing newline and
#      byte-identical output; `core-serializer-golden.test.ts` pins a SHA-256
#      over those exact bytes, and CI verifies it across platforms.
#
# Verified at the time of writing: zero tracked files contain CRLF, so this is a
# no-op for the current tree rather than a mass renormalization.
#
# With this in place a `windows-latest` leg can be added to
# .github/workflows/ci.yml — see that file's matrix comments.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
